        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"You are a strict personal finance and money education curator for StudentSpot, a money education bot for undergraduate and graduate students in India.\\n\\nSTEP 1 - FILTER:\\nFirst strictly filter out any article that is NOT related to:\\n- Personal finance tips and advice\\n- Budgeting and saving money\\n- Debt management and loans\\n- Financial independence and freedom\\n- Money management for students\\n- Investment basics for beginners\\n- Tax planning and savings\\n- Insurance and retirement basics\\n- India personal finance topics\\n\\nSTRICTLY IGNORE and SKIP any article about:\\n- Stock market prices and trading\\n- Cryptocurrency trading\\n- Corporate finance and business\\n- Politics, government, war\\n- Sports, entertainment, movies\\n- Startup funding and VC\\n- General technology\\n- Any non-personal finance topic\\n\\nSTEP 2 - CATEGORIZE:\\nFor each filtered article, read the content carefully and assign the most accurate category based on what the article is actually about. Choose a short clear category name with relevant emoji that truly matches the content. Never hardcode categories.\\n\\nSTEP 3 - WRITE SUMMARY:\\nWrite summary with dynamic subheadings based on article content.\\n\\nUsing ONLY these real articles. Use the EXACT links — do not make up links!\\n\\nArticles:\\n\" + $json.title + \"\\n\" + $json.link + \"\\n\" + $json.contentSnippet + \"\\n\\nFormat EXACTLY like this:\\n\\n*💰 MoneyMentor Daily 💰*\\n\\n*[Category Emoji] [Category Name]*\\n*📌 [Title]*\\n\\n[One clear sentence explaining the update simply]\\n\\n*[Subheading based on content]:\\n• [bullet point]\\n• [bullet point]\\n\\n[Subheading based on content]:\\n• [bullet point]\\n• [bullet point]*\\n\\n🔗 [exact link]\\n\\n*💡 Smart money moves start here!\\n— Student Spot 🎓*\\n\\nRULES:\\n- Only process 100% personal finance and money education related articles\\n- If an article is not related simply skip it completely with no message\\n- Never write any explanation about skipped articles\\n- Never use any heading for skipped articles\\n- Only show articles that passed the filter\\n- If ALL articles are irrelevant send nothing at all\\n- Never hardcode category names\\n- Never hardcode subheadings — pick naturally based on article content\\n- Use 2 to 3 subheadings only as needed\\n- Always use • for bullet points\\n- Category must match actual content\\n- Simple English only\\n- Medium length — not too short not too long\\n- Maximum 1 articles per message Pick top 4 most important and trending articles\\n- Always include exact link\"\n    }\n  ]\n}) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
